# Build products (one shared target/ for every component workspace,
# see .cargo/config.toml).
target/

# macOS and editor noise
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
*.swo

# Local configuration and scratch output
.env
.env.*
out/

# AgentRail session transcripts are local and can grow without bound.
# Durable saga records -- saga.toml, steps/, trajectories/ -- stay tracked;
# losing them would break the handoff between sessions.
#
# BOTH paths matter. `agentrail archive` moves a whole saga, sessions
# included, into .agentrail-archive/, where the first pattern no longer
# matches it. One archived transcript here was 3.1 MB; ../sw-mlpl reports
# that committing these repeatedly took its .git to 2.2 GB and tripped
# GitHub's large-file block.
.agentrail/sessions/
.agentrail-archive/*/sessions/

# Belt and braces. The two patterns above depend on agentrail's current
# directory layout; this one does not. A session transcript is a .jsonl
# and no .jsonl under any agentrail path is ever worth tracking.
.agentrail*/**/*.jsonl

# Model checkpoints and the .spm files derived from them. A TRM
# checkpoint is 27 MB; the DeepSeek R1 1.58-bit quant is ~300 GB.
# GitHub hard-blocks files over 100 MB and wants repositories under
# about 1 GB, so weights live outside the tree and are fetched or
# regenerated. docs/ records where each one came from.
models/
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.gguf

# .spm files are derived artifacts too -- EXCEPT the tiny golden
# fixtures that pin the byte layout, which are the format's contract
# and measured in bytes rather than megabytes.
*.spm
!**/tests/golden/*.spm
